+**Files**: `src/routes/callbacks/reminder.ts`, `src/routes/actions/delivery.ts`, `src/services/reminder-delivery.ts`, `src/security/provider-callback-auth.ts`, `migrations/*_delivery_events.sql`, `tests/unit/provider-callback-auth.test.ts`, `tests/integration/reminder-callback.test.ts`, `tests/integration/action-delivery.test.ts`
+
+## Phase 2: Tests First (TDD)
+
+- [ ] T002 [P] Write a failing unit test suite for raw-payload provider-signature verification.
+
+**Implements**: FR-001 (authenticate callbacks).
+
+**Pattern**: Exercise valid, missing, and invalid signatures against the exact raw callback body. The test must assert that verification returns an authenticated provider identity only for the valid case and does not parse/normalize the body before signing bytes are checked.
+
+**Security**: Obtain the provider secret through the application’s existing test-safe configuration seam; do not hard-code production credentials.
+
+**File**: `tests/unit/provider-callback-auth.test.ts`
+
+- [ ] T003 [P] Write a failing request-role integration test for authenticated callback persistence and replay deduplication.
+
+**Implements**: FR-001, FR-002, FR-003.
+
+**Test Flow**:
+1. Seed an action/reminder owned by workspace A through the normal fixture path.
+2. POST a correctly signed provider callback carrying one provider event id and a delivery status.
+3. Assert one `delivery_events` record is stored with workspace A’s id and the expected status.
+4. Replay the identical callback and assert the response is idempotent and the stored event/status transition remains singular.
+5. POST an invalidly signed callback and assert no event is stored.
+
+**Pattern**: Use the application’s request-role/database fixture rather than a privileged direct database connection for assertions that depend on tenancy.
+
+**File**: `tests/integration/reminder-callback.test.ts`
+
+- [ ] T004 [P] Write a failing request-role integration test for `GET /actions/{id}/delivery` workspace isolation.
+
+**Implements**: FR-004.
+
+**Test Flow**:
+1. Seed an action and delivery event in workspace A.
+2. Request the endpoint as a principal in workspace A and assert the persisted delivery status is returned.
+3. Request the same action id as a principal in workspace B and assert the application’s standard non-disclosure/denial response and no delivery-event payload.
+
+**Security**: The test must use the request role/context used in production so it proves the route’s actual authorization boundary.
+
+**File**: `tests/integration/action-delivery.test.ts`
+
+## Phase 3: Core Implementation (only after all behavior tests fail)
+
+- [ ] T005 Add the `delivery_events` migration with workspace scoping and provider-event idempotency.
+
+**Implements**: FR-002, FR-003.
+
+**Pattern**: Follow the application’s existing migration format and naming convention. Define the event’s action/reminder association, `workspace_id`, provider event id, delivery status, and timestamps required by the existing data conventions. Enforce uniqueness on the provider event identity at the database layer and add indexes/foreign keys consistent with the project’s workspace-scoped tables.
+
+**Security**: Ensure the migration participates in the project’s existing request-role/RLS policy mechanism; it must not create a bypass path for delivery reads.
+
+**File**: `migrations/*_delivery_events.sql`
+
+- [ ] T006 Implement provider callback signature verification as a reusable boundary component.
+
+**Implements**: FR-001.
+
+**Pattern**: Verify the signature against the unmodified raw request body using the configured provider secret and the API’s standard error type. Keep parsing and persistence outside this component so invalid callbacks cannot reach the service layer.
+
+**Testing**: Make the signature test pass without weakening its raw-payload, missing-signature, or invalid-signature cases.
+
+**File**: `src/security/provider-callback-auth.ts`
+
+- [ ] T007 Implement the idempotent callback service that resolves workspace ownership and persists one delivery event.
+
+**Implements**: FR-002, FR-003.
+
+**Pattern**: Resolve the callback target’s workspace from the existing action/reminder relationship, then perform the insert through the application’s normal database service. Convert the uniqueness-conflict path into an idempotent outcome; do not pre-check for an event and then write.
+
+**Testing**: Make the callback test’s first-delivery, replay, persisted-workspace, and invalid-signature non-mutation assertions pass.
+
+**File**: `src/services/reminder-delivery.ts`
+
+- [ ] T008 Implement `POST /callbacks/reminder` as the authenticated callback boundary.
+
+**Implements**: FR-001, FR-002, FR-003.
+
+**Pattern**: Preserve the raw payload long enough for the signature verifier, authenticate before parsing/mutation, pass only verified callback data to the idempotent service, and use the project’s established idempotent success response for a replay. Register the route through the existing API router rather than a second server entry point.
+
+**Security**: Return the established authentication failure response for missing/invalid signatures without revealing workspace or action details.
+
+**File**: `src/routes/callbacks/reminder.ts`
+
+- [ ] T009 Implement workspace-scoped `GET /actions/{id}/delivery`.
+
+**Implements**: FR-004.
+
+**Pattern**: Use the authenticated request role/context to constrain the action and delivery-event lookup to the requester’s workspace. Reuse the API’s normal not-found/forbidden policy consistently; do not load an unscoped event and filter it in memory.
+
+**Testing**: Make the delivery-access test pass for the owning workspace and cross-workspace denial/non-disclosure cases.
+
+**File**: `src/routes/actions/delivery.ts`
